 coordinates, category, aggregate rating with review count and source (Yelp/Tripadvisor/...), and current open status (Open/Closed in the business's local time, with Bing's rendered sentence such as \"Open · Closes 10 PM\"). Results are not filtered by opening hours: to find what is open now, read `open_status` on the rows. Use the ypid with `business` for structured weekly hours.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\nThe provider identifies `results` as the primary payload key.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `address` | string | Single-line street address as Bing prints it. |\n| `category` | string |  |\n| `category_path` | string |  |\n| `image_url` | string |  |\n| `latitude` | number |  |\n| `longitude` | number |  |\n| `maps_url` | string |  |\n| `name` | string |  |\n| `open_hours_text` | string | Bing's rendered status sentence, e.g. \"Open · Closes 10 PM\", \"Closed · Opens tomorrow 7 AM\", \"Closes in 24 mins\" or \"Open 24 hours\". |\n| `open_status` | string | \"Open\" or \"Closed\" at the time of the call in the business's own time, as Bing renders it in the result row; null when Bing shows no hours for the business. |\n| `phone` | string | Display phone, e.g. \"(202) 638-2570\". |\n| `rating` | number | Rating exactly as Bing reports it; scale depends on rating_source (for example Yelp versus ZocDoc). |\n| `rating_count` | number |  |\n| `rating_source` | string | Yelp, Tripadvisor, Foursquare, ... as shown by Bing. |\n| `style_category` | string |  |\n| `website` | string |  |\n| `ypid` | string |  |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so."},"default":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{}}},"description":"Error response; upstream passthrough responses may use provider formats"}},"summary":"Search","tags":["Bing Maps"],"x-aisa-capabilities":{"idempotency":"